      "description": "<p>Police confirm arrest of 37-year-old and 14-year-old boy over alleged assault in Torquay on Sunday night</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Leaders from across the political spectrum have condemned the alleged assault of a One Nation volunteer with a baseball bat outside his home on Victoria’s Surf Coast.</p><p>Police on Tuesday confirmed they arrested a 37-year-old Hampton Park man and a 14-year-old boy over the incident, which occurred at a Torquay home on Sunday night.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/03/one-nation-volunteer-alleged-attack-assault-torquay-victoria-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
